  "awWhatTitle": "What does “PWD” mean?",
  "awWhatBody": "PWD stands for Persons with Disabilities — people who have a long-term physical, sensory, cognitive, or learning condition. Disability is a natural part of human diversity. Use person-first language: say “a person with a disability,” not “a disabled person.” Every learner deserves the same respect and the same chance to learn.",
  "awKindsTitle": "Common kinds of disability",
  "awRespectTitle": "Interacting respectfully",
  "awRespect1": "Speak directly to the person, not to their companion or interpreter.",
  "awRespect2": "Ask before you help — don’t assume someone needs it.",
  "awRespect3": "Be patient and give people time to respond.",
  "awRespect4": "Keep language simple and clear; avoid labels and pity.",
  "awRespect5": "A wheelchair, cane, or guide is personal space — don’t touch it without permission.",
  "awCommTitle": "Communicating accessibly",
  "awCommBody": "Many Deaf and hard-of-hearing Filipinos communicate through Filipino Sign Language (FSL) — a complete language with its own grammar. Captions, plain text, pictures, and sign-language video all make information reach more people. This app teaches vocabulary alongside FSL clips so signing learners are included from the start.",
  "awHelpsTitle": "How FlashLearn PWD helps",
  "awHelps1": "High-contrast and dyslexia-friendly themes for easier reading.",
  "awHelps2": "Adjustable font size, reduced motion, and text-to-speech.",
  "awHelps3": "Filipino Sign Language videos in flashcards and stories.",
  "awHelps4": "Hands-free gaze control — move your head or blink to select.",
